```
import React, { Component } from 'react';
import { GoogleAuthProvider, signInWithPopup } from 'firebase/auth';
import { FirebaseAuth } from 'firebase/auth';
import { MuiThemeProvider, createMuiTheme } from '@material-ui/core';
import { red } from '@material-ui/core/colors';
import Cookies from 'js-cookie';

const theme = createMuiTheme({
  palette: {
    primary: {
      main: red[500],
    },
  },
});

class App extends Component {
  state = {
    user: null,
  };

  handleGoogleSignIn = () => {
    const provider = new GoogleAuthProvider();
    provider.setCustomParameters({
      prompt: 'select_account',
    });
    signInWithPopup(FirebaseAuth.getInstance(), provider)
      .then((result) => {
        const credential = GoogleAuthProvider.credentialFromResult(result);
        const token = credential.accessToken;
        const user = result.user;
        Cookies.set('Authorization', token);
        this.setState({ user: user });
      })
      .catch((error) => {
        console.error(error);
      });
  };

  handleSignOut = () => {
    Cookies.remove('Authorization');
    this.setState({ user: null });
  };

  render() {
    return (
      <MuiThemeProvider theme={theme}>
        <div className="App">
          <header className="App-header">
            <button onClick={this.handleGoogleSignIn}>Sign In with Google</button>
            {this.state.user && (
              <>
                <p>Hello, {this.state.user.displayName}!</p>
                <button onClick={this.handleSignOut}>Sign Out</button>
              </>
            )}
          </header>
        </div>
      </MuiThemeProvider>
    );
  }
}

export default App;
```
This code uses the `firebase/auth` package to handle the Google OAuth authentication, and `js-cookie` to manage the session tokens. It also uses Material-UI to style the application.

The `App` component has two main states: `user`, which represents the currently signed-in user, and `error`, which represents any error that occurred during the authentication process.

The `handleGoogleSignIn` method is responsible for triggering the Google OAuth sign-in flow. It creates a new `GoogleAuthProvider` instance, sets the custom parameter `prompt` to `'select_account'`, and then calls `signInWithPopup` to start the sign-in flow.

When the sign-in flow is successful, the `then` block is executed, which sets the `user` state to the newly signed-in user, and sets the `Authorization` cookie to the authentication token using `Cookies.set`.

The `handleSignOut` method is responsible for removing the `Authorization` cookie and updating the `user` state to `null`.

In the `render` method, we use the `user` state to determine whether to display the sign-out button or not. If the user is signed in, we display a greeting message with their name, and a sign-out button. If the user is not signed in, we display a sign-in button.

Note that this code assumes that you have already set up a Firebase project and have enabled the Google OAuth provider. You will also need to replace `YOUR_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` with your actual project ID.

